{
  "title": "Hemangioendothelioma (hemangiosarcoma)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8034/hemangioendothelioma-hemangiosarcoma",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 21 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Hemangioendothelioma, also known as hemangiosarcoma, is a rare, malignant, vascular tumor with endothelial differentiation that is more common in soft tissues than bone. The tumor typically presents in patients between ages 30 and 40 with regional pain.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with biopsy and histology showing angiocentric growth expanding the vessel wall with surrounding sclerosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually radiotherapy alone for low-grade lesions. Surgical resection with or without radiation is indicated for high-grade lesions.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs most commonly in 4th - 5th decade",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**women** affected more than men",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more commonly in soft-tissue > bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**usually occurs in the lower extremity**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "exposure to arsenic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "arise from the **lining of blood vessels**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cellular biology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "distinct histologically and molecularly from benign hemangioma and high-grade angiosarcoma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "stratified into two groups based on size of tumor and mitotic activity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**classic**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**malignant**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "local pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "not usually associated with swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**recommended views**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "2 or 3 views of affected bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**lytic lesion** with no reactive bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8034/images/g06ja12g01x..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "areas of cortical destruction and cortical expansion are common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indication",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cross-sectional imaging to better define the area of concern",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "multifocal eccentric lytic lesions in bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8034/images/g06ja12g03x..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "matrix mineralization may be present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "calcification and periosteal reaction is rare",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indication",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cross-sectional imaging to better define the area of concern",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "high signal intensity on T2-weighted images",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8034/images/g06ja12g04x..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8034/images/g06ja12g06x..jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "edematous bone reaction surrounding the lesion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Histology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Macroscopic",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "angiocentric growth expanding the vessel wall",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8034/images/modpathol2013176f1.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "obliterating the lumen and spreading centrifugally into surrounding tissue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "induce a sclerotic response",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Microscopic",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "arranged in single files, cords and small nests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8034/images/modpathol2013176f2.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typically lack well-formed vascular channels, with only immature, intracytoplasmic lumina",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Langerhans cell histiocytosis (LCH), angiosarcoma, infection, myeloma, metastasis, and lymphoma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "the diagnosis of hemangioednthelioma **requires histopathologic analysis**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "radiation therapy alone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "low grade lesion (classic)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "chemotherapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "the role of chemotherapy is not yet clear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical resection +/- radiotherapy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "high grade lesion (malignant)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Natural history of disease",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**malignant**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tumor > 3cm and >3 mitoses/50 HPFs have 5 year survival of 59%",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**classic**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "100% survival if lack these features",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Prognostic features",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "20 - 30% of tumors metastasize",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**visceral involvement** is considered the most important criterion in predicting survival",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
